findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config.rs uses from_file which may error, but no test or review finding distinguishes
    NotFound from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer F13 flags that SiemClient::get() leaks full URL in NotFound\
    \ error and notes contradiction with security comments about sanitization. TEA\
    \ also wrote CWE-209 security tests for error display not leaking file paths.\
    \ However, the specific CliError Display leaking via eprintln was not directly\
    \ flagged \u2014 partial catch at best."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection prevention tests for tenant ID (CWE-113).\
    \ Dev implemented HeaderValue::from_str() which rejects CRLF. Reviewer verified\
    \ in V3. However, the deeper issue \u2014 using raw String instead of TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core \u2014 was not flagged."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies like clap_complete, comfy-table, csv,
    dirs, reqwest, toml use direct version strings instead of workspace = true. The
    code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified but the workspace dependency
    pattern was not enforced.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer F7 explicitly flags: ''No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A config
    file with a typo like [sever] is silently ignored.'' Reviewer F11 also flags the
    token field with #[allow(dead_code)] being deserialized but unused. Reviewer requests
    adding deny_unknown_fields before merge.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified vacuously true assertions using is_none() || true
    pattern. The reviewer flagged weak security test assertions (F8) but not this
    specific config test pattern.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. Reviewer F3 flagged vacuous stub handler tests but not this
    specific config test issue.
